# config/os-support.list — THE supported releases. Declared once, here (FR-002).
#
# Every row is a GATE: a release on this list is exercised by the container matrix
# on every change and, where it has a lab machine, proven on that machine before a
# release is declared ready. A release becomes supported by entering this list and
# the gate together; there is no allowed-to-fail tier.
#
# Read by:
#   lib/os.sh                    the run-time gate. A row here is OS_SUPPORT=tested;
#                                a machine of a known family with no row is
#                                `untested` (it runs, with one notice); a machine of
#                                no known family is refused before any change.
#   tests/docker/matrix.sh       its default image list.
#   tests/policy/os-support.sh   fails when the CI matrices or the lab inventory
#                                disagree with this file (SC-006).
#
# FORMAT. One row per release, whitespace-separated, `#` starts a comment:
#
#   family   lib/family/<family>.sh: debian | redhat | suse | arch
#   distro   the os-release ID, exactly
#   release  the matrix form of the release, which is what lib/os.sh compares:
#              Ubuntu and Leap   the exact VERSION_ID      22.04  16.0
#              Debian, EL, Fedora  the major of VERSION_ID  12  9  43
#              Arch              rolling
#   image    the container image the matrix runs, fully qualified
#   lab      yes | no — whether the lab has a real machine of this release
#
# Ubuntu 22.04 has no lab machine: its proof is the container matrix alone.

# family distro        release image                                    lab
debian    debian        12      docker.io/library/debian:12              yes
debian    debian        13      docker.io/library/debian:13              yes
debian    ubuntu        22.04   docker.io/library/ubuntu:22.04           no
debian    ubuntu        24.04   docker.io/library/ubuntu:24.04           yes
debian    ubuntu        26.04   docker.io/library/ubuntu:26.04           yes
redhat    almalinux     9       docker.io/library/almalinux:9            yes
redhat    almalinux     10      docker.io/library/almalinux:10           yes
redhat    rocky         9       docker.io/rockylinux/rockylinux:9        yes
redhat    rocky         10      docker.io/rockylinux/rockylinux:10       yes
redhat    fedora        43      docker.io/library/fedora:43              yes
redhat    fedora        44      docker.io/library/fedora:44              yes
suse      opensuse-leap 16.0    docker.io/opensuse/leap:16.0             yes
arch      arch          rolling docker.io/library/archlinux:latest       yes
